 "briefing": "# Infosys Briefing: Changes from 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Research Status\n\nNo verified changes at Infosys Limited (NSE: INFY, BSE: 500209) could be confirmed for 16 October to 15 November 2026. Every search attempt returned \"Rate limit exceeded,\" and no page was successfully retrieved from any source. The absence of results reflects a failed search, not evidence that Infosys made no announcements in this window. This briefing therefore contains no dated items, and no facts have been inferred or added.\n\n## News\n\nNo verified news items were retrieved for the window. Headlines, press releases, and exchange disclosures were not accessible, so no materiality ranking is possible.\n\n## Product and Service Launches\n\nNo verified product, platform, or service launches were identified for the window. Searches covering AI, agentic AI, Topaz, cloud, cybersecurity, and industry solutions all failed, so the absence of items here is unconfirmed.\n\n## Executive and Notable Hires\n\nNo verified executive appointments, departures, board changes, or notable hires were identified for the window. The status of leadership changes is therefore unknown.\n\n## Deals, Contracts, and Partnerships\n\nNo verified acquisitions, divestitures, client contracts, alliances, or partnerships were identified for the window. Searches for deal announcements, contract wins, and partnerships all failed, so this category is unconfirmed.\n\n## Recommended Verification Before the Meeting\n\nBecause the search tool was unavailable, the following primary sources should be checked directly, filtered to 16 October to 15 November 2026. These links were not accessed during research and are listed only as places to verify.\n\n1. [Infosys Newsroom](https://www.infosys.com/newsroom): press releases for news, launches, hires, and deals.\n2. [Infosys Investors](https://www.infosys.com/investors): stock exchange filings, quarterly materials, and SEC Form 6-K filings.\n3. [NSE Corporate Filings and Announcements](https://www.nseindia.com/companies-listing/corporate-filings-announcements): Regulation 30 disclosures for INFY.\n4. [BSE Corporate Announcements](https://www.bseindia.com/corporates/ann.html): disclosures for scrip code 500209.\n5. [SEC EDGAR](https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/): Infosys Form 6-K filings for the window.\n\nBusiness press (Reuters, Economic Times, Mint, Business Standard, Moneycontrol, and Bloomberg) should be searched for \"Infosys\" within the same date range to capture reported moves that have not yet been formally disclosed.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. Which press releases, stock exchange disclosures, or Form 6-K filings did Infosys issue between 16 October and 15 November 2026, and did any of them change its strategy, guidance, or leadership?\n2. Has Infosys announced or closed any new client contracts, acquisitions, or alliances in the past month, and what are their scale and expected impact on the business?\n3. Have any senior executive or board changes taken effect or been announced in this period, and how do they affect the teams we would be working with?\n\n### Sources\n\n[1] Infosys Newsroom: https://www.infosys.com/newsroom\n[2] Infosys Investors: https://www.infosys.com/investors\n[3] NSE Corporate Filings and Announcements: https://www.nseindia.com/companies-listing/corporate-filings-announcements\n[4] BSE Corporate Announcements: https://www.bseindia.com/corporates/ann.html\n[5] SEC EDGAR Search: https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/",
